Initialize a structured web project for an e-commerce admin panel for the shop **"ELECTRONIC MIKE SUPLIER"**. The goal is to build a modular, scalable, and clean admin system using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

Step 1: Project Structure
Create the following folder structure:

* /project-root

  * index.html (main website)
  * admin.html (admin panel UI)
  * /css/style.css (shared styles)
  * /js/script.js (main website logic)
  * /js/admin.js (admin panel logic)
  * /js/storage.js (localStorage handling functions)
  * /js/auth.js (admin authentication logic)
  * /assets/images (product images)

Step 2: Admin Panel Initialization
In admin.html, create a clean dashboard layout with:

* Header (Admin Panel title + logout button)
* Sidebar (Dashboard, Add Product, Manage Products)
* Main content area (dynamic content sections)

Step 3: Admin Authentication Module
In auth.js:

* Implement simple admin login using a fixed password
* Store admin session in localStorage
* Restrict admin.html access if not logged in
* Add login form UI if not authenticated

Step 4: Storage Module
In storage.js:

* Create reusable functions:

  * getProducts()
  * saveProducts(products)
  * addProduct(product)
  * deleteProduct(index)
* Use localStorage for data persistence

Step 5: Product Management Module
In admin.js:

* Initialize dashboard on load
* Create "Add Product" form (name, price, image URL, description)
* Save product using storage module
* Display product list dynamically
* Add delete button for each product

Step 6: UI Components
Design reusable UI:

* Product cards
* Buttons (Add, Delete)
* Input forms
* Responsive layout

Step 7: Integration with Main Website
Ensure products saved from admin panel are automatically visible in index.html via shared storage (localStorage).

Step 8: Code Quality

* Use clean modular JavaScript (separate concerns)
* Add comments for each function
* Use meaningful variable names
* Avoid inline scripts

Step 9: Security Note
Mention clearly that this admin system is for learning/demo only and not secure for production. Suggest future upgrade to Firebase Authentication and Firestore.

Step 10: Final Output
Generate full working code for:

* admin.html
* css/style.css
* js/admin.js
* js/storage.js
* js/auth.js

Ensure the admin panel is fully functional, clean UI, and ready to integrate with the main website.
